{
  "type": "record",
  "namespace": "deposits.term_deposit",
  "name": "DepositConstituted",
  "doc": "The deposit is opened: principal, the rate-sheet-resolved TAN, and the AT_MATURITY schedule fixed at constitution. Business payload only (ADR-IC-002 §P5); CloudEvents envelope rides in Kafka headers, NOT here. No PII (ADR-PC-004 §P2).",
  "fields": [
    { "name": "deposit_id", "type": { "type": "string", "logicalType": "uuid" }, "doc": "DepositId (Guid)." },
    { "name": "principal_cents", "type": "long", "doc": "Principal as integer EUR cents (Money.Cents, ADR-PC-010 §P1)." },
    { "name": "tan_basis_points", "type": "int", "doc": "Annual nominal rate (TAN) in basis points, resolved from the rate sheet at constitution." },
    { "name": "rate_sheet_version_id", "type": "string", "doc": "The pinned rate-sheet version the TAN was resolved from." },
    { "name": "term_days", "type": "int", "doc": "Term length in days." },
    { "name": "start_date", "type": { "type": "int", "logicalType": "date" }, "doc": "StartDate (DateOnly) as days since epoch." },
    { "name": "maturity_date", "type": { "type": "int", "logicalType": "date" }, "doc": "MaturityDate (DateOnly) as days since epoch." },
    { "name": "interest_variant", "type": "string", "doc": "Interest variant discriminator (e.g. AT_MATURITY)." },
    { "name": "auto_renewal_policy", "type": "string", "doc": "Auto-renewal policy discriminator." },
    { "name": "payment_period_months", "type": "int", "default": 0, "doc": "PERIODIC coupon cadence in months (1 monthly, 3 quarterly); 0 for AT_MATURITY/ADVANCE. Additive with a default so pre-F.1 AT_MATURITY records that never carried it still decode (forward-only schema evolution, ADR-IC-002)." },
    { "name": "product_code", "type": "string", "default": "", "doc": "The catalogue product code (e.g. dpz_pt_12m_juros_venc) — the STRUCTURAL product identifier the rate sheet prices (ConstituteDepositCommand.ProductId), the queryable 'which product is this' dimension that rate_sheet_version_id (a price/version key, one-to-many to products) cannot provide. Structural, NOT PII (ADR-PC-004 §P2). Additive with a default so pre-v794 records that never carried it still decode as the empty default (forward-only schema evolution, ADR-IC-002 §P3); those historical deposits are NOT back-fillable from the log because the code is discarded at constitution and rate_sheet_version_id→product is one-to-many. Prospective only (bd babelstone-v794)." },
    { "name": "role", "type": "string", "default": "", "doc": "The pricing role the rate sheet priced the TAN against (ConstituteDepositCommand.Role, e.g. 'standard') — a STRUCTURAL pricing dimension, NOT PII (ADR-PC-004 §P2). Persisted so the engine can re-resolve the SAME (product, role) rate at auto-renewal entirely from the closing deposit, keeping product-family knowledge out of the orchestrator (ADR-IC-003 §A7). Additive with a default so pre-mtto.5 records that never carried it still decode as the empty default (forward-only schema evolution, ADR-IC-002 §P3); a renewal of such a deposit defaults the empty role to 'standard' (the v1 default role). Prospective only (bd babelstone-mtto.5)." },
    { "name": "funding_account", "type": "string", "default": "", "doc": "An OPAQUE funding-account TOKEN — a REFERENCE the engine resolves internally, NEVER an IBAN/cleartext account identifier (ADR-PC-004 §P2: references are allowed on the durable bus; PII is not). The legacy current account the principal was debited / the renewal rollover is debited (ConstituteDepositCommand.FundingAccount). Persisted so the engine can settle the auto-renewal rollover debit against the SAME funding reference entirely from the closing deposit, keeping product/funding knowledge out of the orchestrator (ADR-IC-003 §A7). Additive with a default so pre-mtto.5 records that never carried it still decode as the empty default (forward-only schema evolution, ADR-IC-002 §P3); a renewal of such a deposit fails loud rather than debit an empty funding reference. Prospective only (bd babelstone-mtto.5)." },
    { "name": "min_withdrawal_cents", "type": "long", "default": 0, "doc": "F.12 partial-withdrawal gate PINNED at constitution: the smallest partial withdrawal the product allows, in integer EUR cents (PartialWithdrawalPolicy.MinWithdrawalCents). 0 ⇒ no minimum. Resolved from the product config's partial_withdrawal block and stamped here so the policy a live deposit is subject to is fixed at constitution — a config edit cannot retroactively change it (the per-instance pinning the rate/term get, ADR-PC-009). Structural config, NOT PII (ADR-PC-004 §P2). Additive with a default so pre-F.12 records that never carried it decode as 0 = Unrestricted (forward-only schema evolution, ADR-IC-002 §P3). Prospective only (bd babelstone-k6r8.8/qze9)." },
    { "name": "min_remaining_balance_cents", "type": "long", "default": 0, "doc": "F.12 partial-withdrawal gate PINNED at constitution: the smallest principal that may remain on deposit after a partial withdrawal, in integer EUR cents (PartialWithdrawalPolicy.MinRemainingBalanceCents). 0 ⇒ no floor. Same pinning + additive-default semantics as min_withdrawal_cents. Structural config, NOT PII. Prospective only (bd babelstone-k6r8.8/qze9)." },
    { "name": "lockup_period_days", "type": "int", "default": 0, "doc": "F.12 partial-withdrawal gate PINNED at constitution: the lock-up window in days from constitution during which no partial withdrawal is allowed (PartialWithdrawalPolicy.LockupPeriodDays). 0 ⇒ no lock-up. A duration in days, not money. Same pinning + additive-default semantics as min_withdrawal_cents. Structural config, NOT PII. Prospective only (bd babelstone-k6r8.8/qze9)." },
    { "name": "product_config_version", "type": "string", "default": "", "doc": "The product-config generation this deposit was constituted under, PINNED per-event (ADR-PC-009 §A2): a content-hash version (sha256:<hex>) the engine resolves from the product config in the SAME constitution transaction (ADR-PC-008 §S2) and stamps here — a PAYLOAD-shaped pin like rate_sheet_version_id, NOT an envelope column like pack_version. Lets a replay prove which product-config generation governed the deposit (REPLAY_PIN_PER_EVENT). Structural version string, NOT PII (ADR-PC-004 §P2). Additive with a default so pre-pin records decode as the empty default (forward-only schema evolution, ADR-IC-002 §P3); '' when no product-config store is wired or the config carried no version. The product-config YAMLs are still static deploy-time artefacts — a versioned POST /v1/product-configs registry is later work (bd babelstone-fk7m.9 follow-up). Prospective only." }
  ]
}
